  "title": "Kingdom of Dahomey",
  "summary": "Dahomey was a Fon kingdom centred on Abomey in what is now Benin. After taking Allada in 1724 and Ouidah in 1727 it had direct access to the Atlantic, and its rulers sold captives to European traders until 1852. It fielded the Agojie, a women's regiment that guarded the palaces and fought. France defeated it in 1892–1894.",
